{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/connector at b80502a6259d0f91308b41ba79cfa93b97ab8a57 on request/github-connector-render. Successor to 4eb2dc81fd837b4cd7e3ad5b8aeaf21e096ff12e, which pointed at 68c0f42f before codex's four findings.\n\nCloses all four. The charter now says what the connector may do, not only where: a charter declaring no operations authorizes observation alone, so the outbound half cannot be reached by a charter written for reading.\n\nThe command no longer treats supplied as true. It required a request, an artifact and a commit; three well-formed strings naming records with nothing to do with each other would have opened a pull request citing a request that does not govern that artifact, or an artifact that names different code. A reader on GitHub cannot tell, and a pull request cannot be superseded. The relationship is now checked against the projection before anything is posted — both events present, neither retired nor stale, the artifact naming exactly the commit being rendered, and resting on the governing request — with a separate refusal for each, because an unknown event, a stale one, and one describing other code are different mistakes.\n\nOpen() also accepted a created pull request carrying no usable number or url, which would have left a promise looking kept with nothing able to close it.\n\nTwo comments overclaimed and now say what is true. The marker does not exclude the connector's own writing from its reading and should not: filtering observations on a string any GitHub user can type would let an author hide an issue by pasting it, turning a label into a denial vector. What actually excludes the outbound half is that the inbound half skips pull requests. Opening a pull request is not idempotent; the real asymmetry is that neither direction reads the other's writing.\n\nAlso removes a built binary committed by accident in the predecessor commit, and ignores the shape that produces it.\n\ngo vet and the full suite pass, worktree clean at this head.","body":{"branch":"request/github-connector-render","commit":"b80502a6259d0f91308b41ba79cfa93b97ab8a57","head":"b80502a6259d0f91308b41ba79cfa93b97ab8a57","path":"internal/connector"}}